The 'Mined courses.json' file is the output file from scraper.py containing mined course data from ttb.utoronto.ca/. 

## Structure
Array of course objects. Fields are inconsistent across courses - not every course has every key. All values are strings, with the exception of 'Lectures' which is an array of lecture objects containing lecture data.

### Top-level keys
['Architecture Breadth Category:', 'Arts & Science Breadth Category:', 'Availability', 'Campus', 'Co-requisites:', 'Course Name', 'Credit Value:', 'Delivery Mode', 'Department:', 'Description:', 'Engineering Elective Category:', 'Enrolment Controls', 'Exclusions:', 'Faculty / Division:', 'First Term\nDay/Time', 'First Term\nLocation', 'Instructor(s)', 'Lectures', 'Note:', 'Notes:', 'Pre-requisites:', 'Recommended Preparation:', 'Second Term\nDay/Time', 'Second Term\nLocation', 'Session', 'University of Toronto Mississauga Distribution Category:', 'University of Toronto Scarborough Breadth Category:', 'Waitlist']

### Lectures (nested array within each course)
['Availability', 'Day/Time', 'Delivery Mode', 'Enrolment Controls', 'First Term\nDay/Time', 'First Term\nLocation', 'Instructor(s)', 'Lecture Code', 'Location', 'Notes:', 'Second Term\nDay/Time', 'Second Term\nLocation', 'Waitlist']

## Notes / known quirks
- 'Note:' vs 'Notes:' - for the most part used interchangeably, but 'Notes:' is also used for changes such as a cancelled lecture
- Trailing colons on most keys reflect the source site's raw labels
- Some string fields may contain non-ASCII characters


